# source: SYNTHETIC
# title: The feared case: SDP c= names 127.0.0.3 but the station really sends media from 127.0.0.1
# verdict: DIFFERS
# basis: the open question the live capture must settle: does the real station send RTP from its SDP c= address?
# reason: if the station's RTP source differs from its SDP c=, gate-sip plays the audio and Portico silently drops it (rtpIn stays 0). Needs a live capture

>>> send
INVITE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKinv1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 INVITE
Contact: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>
Content-Type: application/sdp
Max-Forwards: 70

v=0
o=- 0 0 IN IP4 {{STIP}}
s=-
c=IN IP4 127.0.0.3
t=0 0
m=audio {{RTP}} RTP/AVP 8
a=rtpmap:8 PCMA/8000
.
>>> recv
>>> answer
>>> recv
>>> send
ACK sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKack1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 ACK
Max-Forwards: 70
.
>>> rtp from=station n=3 pt=8
>>> state
